Why these changes work:
 * Strict DTO Mapping: By using LhoTransferPayloadDto in the service, you ensure the data is validated before it ever touches the database.
 * Raw Value Handling: @JsonRawValue is the most efficient way to handle JSON in a legacy String/CLOB column. It avoids "double-escaping" (those annoying \" quotes).
 * Precision: Since your DTO uses BigDecimal, Jackson will respect your 20-digit numbers and 4 decimal places during the writeValueAsString process.
One Final Tip: Global Precision
To make sure those BigDecimal values don't turn into scientific notation (1.1E8) when you save them as a string, add this to your application.properties:
spring.jackson.serialization.write-bigdecimal-as-plain=true

